## 3. CSRA v5.0
Principle 1: Reduce risk from the inside out
- 1.1 Least privilege
- 1.2 Eliminate unnecessary security controls
- 1.3 Isolation
Principle 2: Increase mission assurance through resilience
- 2.1 Deny by default
- 2.2 Assume breach
- 2.3 Recover
Principle 3: Enable modernization
- 3.1 Integrate ICAM
- 3.2 Establish and enforce data tagging
- 3.3 Accelerate movement to secure cloud services
- 3.4 Standardize and streamline cybersecurity data analytics

Outcomes ZTA: eliminar/reduzir Persistence, Privilege Escalation, Lateral Movement
- Authenticated and authorized access to all resources
- Access control enforcement based on multiple sources of authoritative data
- Automated security responses enable dynamic changes to security controls

Atividades A.1 a A.8:
- A.1 Identify: Identify users, devices, services
- A.2 Manage: Manage users, devices, configuration
- A.3 Control: Macro/micro segment network + environment
- A.4 Protect: Tag data, encrypt data, enforce security policies
- A.5 Detect: Detect anomalous behavior, inspect traffic content + measurements
- A.6 Analyze: Log inspection results, analyze event data
- A.7 Automate: Automate policy-based + event-based responses
- A.8 Orchestrate: Integrate threat intelligence + automated workflows

Capabilities C.1 a C.5:
- C.1 Identify: User enumeration, Device enumeration
- C.2 Protect: Authentication and authorization, Data protection, Network protection, Application security
- C.3 Detect: Continuous monitoring
- C.4 Respond: Cyberspace defense
- C.5 Recover: Cyberspace survivability

Enhancements:
- 4.1 Cloud: CNAP, CNSS Policy 32, FedRAMP, CC SRG
- 4.2 Cross Domain: Information Exchange Security, JCA 6.3.1
- 4.3 Control Systems: ICS / SCADA, 7 camadas ICS, MCCS / MC-FRCS, OT prioriza availability
- 4.4 Space Systems: SCDRA, Cyber for Defensive Space Control

## 4. Cruzamento 7 Pilares
- 1. User - XA: Identity & Policy - Pode: vincular identidade, credenciais, contexto e decisao a registros - Falta: inventario, MFA, federacao, PAM, autenticacao continua, menor privilegio
- 2. Device - XA: Identidade de dispositivo - Pode: registrar identidade declarada e associar a execucao - Falta: inventario, postura, autorizacao real-time, UEM/MDM, EDR/XDR
- 3. Applications/Workloads - XA: Execution Observability - Pode: associar app, versao, workload, politica e execucao - Falta: inventario apps, dev seguro, risco software, autorizacao continua
- 4. Data - XA: Evidence Collection, Vault, criptografia - Pode: preservar payloads, proveniencia, hashes, assinaturas, manifests - Falta: catalogo, classificacao, monitoramento, DLP, direitos, controle acesso
- 5. Networks/Environments - XA: Trust Boundaries - Pode: registrar fronteiras, origem, destino, contexto - Falta: SDN, fluxos, macro e microsegmentacao aplicadas
- 6. Orchestration/Automation - XA: Policy Engine, Decision Orchestrator - Pode: registrar politicas, decisoes, resultados - Falta: PDP operacional, SOAR, resposta incidentes, SOC
- 7. Analytics/Visibility - XA: Logs, auditoria, GT7, GT96-R - Pode: correlacionar eventos, decisoes, evidencias - Falta: SIEM, UEBA, threat intel, analytics, cobertura logs

Leitura: mais direto em Data, Orchestration/Automation, Analytics/Visibility. Nos demais, so camada de evidencia, nao substitui controles.

## 5. Pilares DoD vs E3-E8
- Pilares DoD = dominios de capacidades
- E3-E8 = estados do ciclo de evidencias XA-TRUST
- E3 EXECUTION: evidencia de que execucao ocorreu no escopo declarado
- E4 PROVENANCE: vinculo de origem e proveniencia
- E5 CRYPTOGRAPHIC BINDING: vinculacao criptografica
- E6 INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION: verificacao independente
- E7 VERIFIED(CLAIM-X): resultado verificado limitado a claim especifica
- E8 Escopo global: exige criterios globais, reconstrucao independente e politica
- E7 de 1 execucao nao significa pilar inteiro atendido. Crosswalk nao promove para E6/E7.

